cff-version: 1.2.0
type: software
title: "NERO-VLA: an offline backbone benchmark on real-robot manipulation data"
message: "If you use this benchmark or its evaluation protocol, please cite it."
abstract: >-
  Seven vision-language-action backbones (pi0, pi0.5, GR00T N1.5, GR00T N1.7,
  OpenVLA-OFT, SmolVLA, ACT) fine-tuned on the same 131-episode real-robot
  manipulation dataset and compared by open-loop action-chunk mean absolute
  error on a leak-free 20-episode held-out split. The split, the frozen
  evaluation anchors and every backbone's predictions are committed, so the
  leaderboard reproduces byte-for-byte with numpy alone -- no GPU, dataset or
  checkpoint required. The repository also contains the pi0.5 real-robot
  deployment line the dataset came from. Note this is a recipe-level
  comparison rather than a controlled architecture A/B, and no checkpoint has
  been evaluated in closed loop on hardware; see docs/CAVEATS.md.
authors:
  - name: "CodeChildCZJ"
    alias: "CodeChildCZJ"
repository-code: "https://github.com/CodeChildCZJ/nero-vla"
license: Apache-2.0
date-released: "2026-08-07"
keywords:
  - vision-language-action
  - robot-learning
  - imitation-learning
  - manipulation
  - benchmark
  - reproducibility
